## Directory Naming Patterns

### Main Directories
```bash
# Good: Clear and descriptive directory names
internal/          # Internal application code
tests/             # Test files and infrastructure
examples/          # Example configurations
tools/             # Development tools
docs/              # Documentation
scripts/           # Build and deployment scripts
build/             # Build artifacts
coverage/          # Coverage reports

# Bad: Unclear or inconsistent directory names
src/               # Too generic
test/              # Singular
example/           # Singular
tool/              # Singular
doc/               # Singular
script/            # Singular
bin/               # Too generic
cov/               # Abbreviated
```

### Internal Package Directories
```bash
# Good: Domain-specific package names
internal/config/   # Configuration management
internal/ssh/      # SSH operations
internal/facts/    # Fact collection
internal/actions/  # Action management
internal/machines/ # Machine management
internal/templates/ # Template processing
internal/variables/ # Variable management
internal/secrets/  # Secret management
internal/schemas/  # Schema validation
internal/types/    # Type definitions
internal/interfaces/ # Interface definitions
internal/logging/  # Logging management
internal/cli/      # Command-line interface

# Bad: Unclear or inconsistent package names
internal/conf/     # Abbreviated
internal/ssh_client/ # Redundant
internal/fact/     # Singular
internal/action/   # Singular
internal/machine/  # Singular
internal/template/ # Singular
internal/variable/ # Singular
internal/secret/   # Singular
internal/schema/   # Singular
internal/type/     # Singular
internal/interface/ # Singular
internal/log/      # Abbreviated
internal/command/  # Unclear purpose
```

